│     The patch is submitted (2 files, 6917 bytes).                            │
│                                                                              │
│     **What changed:**                                                        │
│     -   **`fastapi/exception_handlers.py`:** Added `_extract_context` (which │
│ finds the route, method, file and line number from the traceback), and the   │
│ three `_forward_*_validation_error` functions.                               │
│     -   **`fastapi/exceptions.py`:** `ResponseValidationError` now has a     │
│ cached `_get_context()` and `_extract_context()` that it calls.              │
│                                                                              │
│     **What I did not confirm:**                                              │
│     -   The validation-exception tests                                       │
│ (`tests/test_tutorial/test_validation_exceptions.py`) ran, but they reported │
│ "no tests ran," so I did not verify the change against existing tests.       │
│     -   I did not run the benchmark from the PR description.                 │
│                                                                              │
│     The context is built once per exception instance and attached as         │
│ `__cause__` on the forwarded exception, so it is not sent in the HTTP        │
│ response. The `RequestValidationError` context is still not attached to the  │
│ exception object itself, so its `__str__` does not include it. I left that   │
│ as the issue did not specify which exception's `__str__` should carry the    │
│ context.                                                                     │
